> factor x^4 - 1
  ucas: factor x^4 - 1
factor x^4 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^4 + 4
  ucas: factor x^4 + 4
factor x^4 + 4
  = (x^2 + 2x + 2)*(x^2 - 2x + 2)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^5 - x
  ucas: factor x^5 - x
factor x^5 - x
  = x*(x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor (x^2+2*x+1)^3
  ucas: factor (x^2+2*x+1)^3
factor (x^2 + 2x + 1)^3
  = (x + 1)^6
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> gcd x^4-1, x^3-1
gcd x^4 - 1, x^3 - 1
  = x - 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> lcm x^2-1, x^2-x
lcm x^2 - 1, x^2 - x
  = x*(x - 1)*(x + 1)
    = x^3 - x
  check: both divide it exactly
> resultant x^2-2, x^2-3 in x
resultant x^2 - 2, x^2 - 3
  in x: 1
  nonzero: no common root
  check: lc(P)^deg(Q) * product of Q over the roots of P = 1 (agrees)
> discriminant x^3+p*x+q in x
discriminant x^3 + p*x + q
  in x (degree 3): -4p^3 - 27q^2
    = -(4p^3 + 27q^2)
  check: at sample values of the coefficients the numeric polynomial's discriminant is -26.133412, the formula gives -26.133412 (agrees)
> quo x^5-1, x-1 in x
quo x^5 - 1, x - 1
  = x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1
  (in x: P = Q*quotient + remainder, deg remainder < 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> rem x^5-1, x^2-1 in x
rem x^5 - 1, x^2 - 1
  = x - 1
  (in x: P = Q*quotient + remainder, deg remainder < 2)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> divide x^5-1 by x^2-1
  ucas: divide x^5-1 by x^2-1
divide x^5 - 1, x^2 - 1
  quotient x^3 + x, remainder x - 1
  (in x: P = Q*quotient + remainder, deg remainder < 2)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> apart 1/(x^2-1) in x
apart 1/(x^2 - 1)
  = 1/(2(x - 1)) - 1/(2(x + 1))
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> solve x^2 = 4 for x
  ucas: solve x^2 = 4 for x
solve x^2 = 4 for x
  x = -2
  x = 2
  check: each solution substituted (2 values): residual 0
> solve x^2 = -1 for x
  ucas: solve x^2 = -1 for x
solve x^2 = -1 for x
  no real solution
  (and 2 complex solutions)
> simplify (x^2-1)/(x-1)
  ucas: simplify (x^2-1)/(x-1)
simplify (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1)
  = x + 1
  holds where x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> expand (x+1)^10
  ucas: expand (x+1)^10
expand (x + 1)^10
  = x^10 + 10x^9 + 45x^8 + 120x^7 + 210x^6 + 252x^5 + 210x^4 + 120x^3 + 45x^2 + 10x + 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
